{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Hurry.</b> Because there was need to travel as far as Sodom that same day." "<b>Three se'ah of flour.</b> And from three se'ah of flour you produce three tenths [of an ephah] of fine flour for these three men. Flour — Rashi explained as the starch of cooks, from the expression פת עמילה. Another interpretation: his oven held three se'ah, and he commanded to fill his oven completely, as our Sages said: bread bakes well when the oven is full." "<b>Knead.</b> It is written ובלוט, and it is written ומצות אפה — from here that the woman kneads and the man bakes." "<b>And make cakes.</b> Because they were pressed to be on their way to carry out their mission and could not delay until it should leaven."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:36.826045520Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}